;; repr/haskell's print level's classes for bin/reap (the REAP row of Haskell; test/reap/cells.edn's :haskell :print): the text level's known
;; differences, in goi's format. Since HES93 (a) (the user, 2026-11-17) the cell's own check, the native reader's verdict (the text
;; printed back byte for byte, test/haskell/roundtrip-ghc-9.14.1-text-known.edn), has none; the classes below take the helper's
;; verdict's (test/haskell/roundtrip-ghc-9.14.1-text-tree-known.edn: the module printed back byte for byte in every case, the difference
;; GHC's trees of mode :full outside the module view), the source reported beside the cell, out of its counts. A module is in the first class whose :match finds its
;; "RESULT REASON". Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :module-view-comments
  :title "a header's comments outside the module view"
  :kind :design
  :why "the three modules that #include \"CTypes.h\", a header with Haskell comments: the original's tree in mode :full holds the header's comments (spans in include/CTypes.h), which the module view (SPEC 2.8, S5) leaves out with the header's other lines, so GHC attaches the module's own documentation otherwise; the printed text is byte-identical"
  :decided "R3; SPEC 2.8, S5"
  :match [#"include/CTypes.h's comments"]}
 {:id :module-view-include
  :title "a CPP #include of Haskell source"
  :kind :design
  :why "the module's text is another file's (a CPP #include of Haskell source: bytestring's ReadInt and ReadNat, filepath's and os-string's Posix and Windows modules): outside the module view, whose conversion in mode :full names the other file's lines; the printed text is byte-identical"
  :decided "R5; SPEC 2.8, S5; HR18"
  :match [#"another file's, a CPP #include of Haskell source"]}
 ;; DECISION 1 (a) of queue 325: the own interface level's known differences of the layout layout
 ;; (test/haskell/roundtrip-ghc-9.14.1-layout-iface-own-known.edn)
 {:id :own-iface-srcloc-column
  :title "a CallStack SrcLoc's column in an own interface's unfolding"
  :kind :design
  :why "the own interface of a module whose unfolding builds a CallStack's SrcLoc (HasCallStack) holds the call's column as an Int# literal; the printed module keeps the original's lines, not its columns, and the comparison normalizes the spans' columns, not a SrcLoc's arguments (GHC's interface level normalizes those columns)"
  :decided "queue 325, DECISION 1 (a)"
  :match [#"interface: a CallStack's SrcLoc column in an unfolding"]}
 ;; :own-iface-span-lines removed 2026-11-22 (no row: the printer keeps a type's closing ) on its line, :hs/close)
]
